---
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import Icon from "../components/icons/Icon.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Roadmap from "../components/icons/glyphs/Roadmap.astro";
import Capability from "../components/icons/glyphs/Capability.astro";
import Assure from "../components/icons/glyphs/Assure.astro";
import Loop from "../components/icons/glyphs/Loop.astro";
import AlignTarget from "../components/icons/glyphs/AlignTarget.astro";
import Network from "../components/icons/glyphs/Network.astro";
import Dialogue from "../components/icons/glyphs/Dialogue.astro";
import Charter from "../components/icons/glyphs/Charter.astro";
import lmiLogo from "../../brand/assets/logos/lmi/LMI-LOGO-702_MAIN-R1_TRANSPARENT.svg";
import "../styles/about.css";
---

<Layout
  title="About EQUIBT | Operational improvement that holds"
  description="EQUIBT is an operational improvement advisory. We build the capability, systems and governance that keep improvement in place after we leave."
>
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <!-- 1. HERO -->
    <section class="about-hero about-reveal">
      <div class="about-hero-inner">
        <div class="about-hero-content">
          <div class="eyebrow">ABOUT</div>
          <h1>We make operational improvement hold.</h1>
          <p class="about-hero-subhead">EQUIBT is an operational improvement advisory. We work with complex service organisations across Australia to build the capability, systems and governance that keep improvement in place after we leave.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="about-hero-art" aria-hidden="true">
          <span><Icon name="hero-about" /></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 2. THE PROBLEM WE SOLVE -->
    <section class="about-section beige about-reveal">
      <div class="about-inner">
        <div class="about-head">
          <div class="eyebrow">THE PROBLEM WE SOLVE</div>
          <h2 class="about-title">Most improvement programmes produce results. Fewer produce results that last.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="about-callout">
          <p class="about-callout-lead">The number one failure mode of operational improvement is not bad methodology.</p>
          <p>It is abandonment.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="about-prose">
          <p>Most programmes follow the same arc. A firm arrives, runs a diagnostic, designs solutions, runs a pilot. The results look good. The firm leaves. Twelve months later the operation has drifted back, sometimes further back, because the programme disrupted a stable operation without building what replaces it.</p>
          <p>That is not a methodology problem. The frameworks are rigorous. The problem is that none of them was designed with exit in mind.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="about-answer-wrap">
          <div class="about-answer">
            <p class="about-answer-lead">We built EQUIBT around a different model.</p>
            <p>Every engagement is scoped from the outset to end with your team running the improved operation independently, without us in the room.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 3. WHY EQUIBT -->
    <section class="about-section white about-reveal">
      <div class="about-inner">
        <div class="about-head">
          <div class="eyebrow">WHY EQUIBT</div>
          <h2 class="about-title">What makes improvement hold in your team.</h2>
          <p>Plenty of firms can run a diagnostic and design a fix. The difference is what survives after the engagement ends. Three things set our work apart.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="about-cols">
          <div class="about-col">
            <span class="about-col-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><Roadmap /></span>
            <h3>Sustainment, not just delivery.</h3>
            <p>You get an exit plan from day one, with the exit criteria agreed before the work starts. We do not move to the next phase until the current one is embedded in how your team operates.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="about-col">
            <span class="about-col-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><Capability /></span>
            <h3>Capability at the centre.</h3>
            <p>You leave the engagement able to run the improved operation yourselves. We measure success by what your team can do once we go, not by what we delivered while we were there. Capability transfer is the point, not an add-on.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="about-col">
            <span class="about-col-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><Assure /></span>
            <h3>Governance that runs itself.</h3>
            <p>You keep the controls that keep the gain. Process architecture, control plans, dashboards and escalation protocols are not closing paperwork, they are the mechanism that holds the improvement in place.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 4. WHAT WE BELIEVE -->
    <section class="about-section beige about-reveal">
      <div class="about-inner">
        <div class="about-head">
          <div class="eyebrow">WHAT WE BELIEVE</div>
          <h2 class="about-title">Four things we will not negotiate on.</h2>
          <p>These are not preferences. They are the non-negotiables that shape every engagement we take.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="about-rows">
          <div class="about-row">
            <p class="about-row-label">Measurement before intervention.</p>
            <p class="about-row-body">We do not accept anecdotes about where the problem is. We measure it. Every engagement starts with a quantified baseline. Opinion without data is not a starting point, it is a bias.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="about-row">
            <p class="about-row-label">Root cause before solution.</p>
            <p class="about-row-body">We do not design solutions until we have isolated the cause. Addressing symptoms is maintenance, not improvement, and a good solution to the wrong problem wastes budget and goodwill.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="about-row">
            <p class="about-row-label">Context shapes method.</p>
            <p class="about-row-body">We keep the method constant and change how we apply it. The questions we ask in financial services are not the questions we ask in government. Generic application is not rigour.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="about-row">
            <p class="about-row-label">AI-ready, not AI-naive.</p>
            <p class="about-row-body">We treat AI as an accelerant, not a replacement for operational rigour, and only when the process is stable, the governance is in place, and the team understands what the model is doing. We do not sell automation into unstable operations.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 5. OUR STORY -->
    <section class="about-section white about-reveal">
      <div class="about-inner">
        <div class="about-head">
          <div class="eyebrow">OUR STORY</div>
          <h2 class="about-title">Equipped to make it hold.</h2>
          <p>A few things worth knowing about how we work, and where the name came from.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="about-rows">
          <div class="about-row story">
            <div class="about-story-head">
              <span class="about-story-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><Loop /></span>
              <p class="about-row-label">Long enough to know what holds.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="about-row-body">We have been at this long enough to learn that an improvement only counts if it survives our exit.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="about-row story">
            <div class="about-story-head">
              <span class="about-story-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><Capability /></span>
              <p class="about-row-label">Say it like "equipped".</p>
            </div>
            <p class="about-row-body">EQUIBT is a made-up word, and the job it names: we equip your team to run the improved operation without us. The domain was free, too.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="about-row story">
            <div class="about-story-head">
              <span class="about-story-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><AlignTarget /></span>
              <p class="about-row-label">We say no a lot.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="about-row-body">We do not consult on everything. We focus on operational performance in complex service organisations, and we say no to the rest.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="about-row story">
            <div class="about-story-head">
              <span class="about-story-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><Network /></span>
              <p class="about-row-label">In it to deliver it.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="about-row-body">We are not a body shop. We do not outsource our talent, and our operators are part of the firm, here for the long term. Each one adds their own spice to the brand.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="about-row story">
            <div class="about-story-head">
              <span class="about-story-glyph" aria-hidden="true"><Dialogue /></span>
              <p class="about-row-label">Grown on WOMBAT.</p>
            </div>
            <p class="about-row-body">Word Of Mouth, Buy And Tell. Our clients send us the next one.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 6. LMI HANDOVER (story-framed: why we built LMI) -->
    <section class="about-section beige about-lmi about-reveal">
      <div class="about-inner">
        <div class="eyebrow">OUR TRAINING DIVISION</div>
        <h2 class="about-title">Build the capability in-house.</h2>
        <p class="about-lmi-copy">We started Lean Methods Institute for the clients who wanted to build the capability themselves, not rent it. It is our specialist training division: the same Lean and AI methods we run inside an engagement, taught to your team through structured courses, so the improvement keeps going after we step out. Working with us to build capability is the point, not an add-on.</p>
        <a href="https://leanmethods.com.au" class="about-lmi-logo-link" aria-label="Lean Methods Institute">
          <img src={lmiLogo.src} class="about-lmi-logo-img" alt="Lean Methods Institute" loading="lazy" />
        </a>
        <a href="https://leanmethods.com.au" class="btn-text"><span class="link-label">Explore training at Lean Methods Institute</span> <span class="ar">&rsaquo;</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 7. CLIENT LOGO WALL -->
    <section class="about-section white about-reveal">
      <div class="about-inner about-logos">
        <div class="eyebrow">CLIENTS</div>
        <h2>Worked across complex, regulated operating environments.</h2>
        <div class="about-logo-marks" aria-label="Selected client logos">
          <img class="about-logo" src="/assets/logos/clients/logo-01.svg" alt="" loading="lazy">
          <img class="about-logo" src="/assets/logos/clients/logo-02.svg" alt="" loading="lazy">
          <img class="about-logo" src="/assets/logos/clients/logo-03.svg" alt="" loading="lazy">
          <img class="about-logo" src="/assets/logos/clients/logo-04.svg" alt="" loading="lazy">
          <img class="about-logo" src="/assets/logos/clients/logo-05.svg" alt="" loading="lazy">
          <img class="about-logo" src="/assets/logos/clients/logo-06.svg" alt="" loading="lazy">
          <img class="about-logo" src="/assets/logos/clients/logo-07.svg" alt="" loading="lazy">
          <img class="about-logo" src="/assets/logos/clients/logo-08.svg" alt="" loading="lazy">
          <img class="about-logo" src="/assets/logos/clients/logo-09.svg" alt="" loading="lazy">
          <img class="about-logo" src="/assets/logos/clients/logo-10.svg" alt="" loading="lazy">
          <img class="about-logo" src="/assets/logos/clients/logo-11.svg" alt="" loading="lazy">
          <img class="about-logo" src="/assets/logos/clients/logo-12.svg" alt="" loading="lazy">
          <img class="about-logo" src="/assets/logos/clients/logo-13.svg" alt="" loading="lazy">
          <img class="about-logo" src="/assets/logos/clients/logo-14.svg" alt="" loading="lazy">
          <img class="about-logo" src="/assets/logos/clients/logo-15.svg" alt="" loading="lazy">
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 8. CLOSING CTA (light, copy left + motif right) -->
    <section class="about-section beige about-cta about-reveal">
      <div class="about-inner about-cta-grid">
        <div class="about-cta-copy">
          <div class="eyebrow">WORK WITH US</div>
          <h2>Start with the problem that won't stay fixed.</h2>
          <p>Tell us about the improvement that never held, or the problem that keeps coming back after every attempt. We will look at it with you and say straight whether it is a fixable process gap, and whether we are the right firm to fix it. You will hear back from an operator, not an auto-reply.</p>
          <a href="/contact/" class="btn-primary">Get in touch</a>
        </div>
        <div class="about-cta-art" aria-hidden="true">
          <!-- closing motif: line-art at interim weight — page artwork swaps in here later (artwork-authority, EQT-274/275) -->
          <Charter />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />

  <script>
    function initialiseAboutReveals() {
      const reduceMotion = window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;
      const sections = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll(".about-reveal"));
      if (reduceMotion || !("IntersectionObserver" in window)) return;
      document.documentElement.classList.add("about-reveal-enabled");
      const observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
        entries.forEach((entry) => {
          if (!entry.isIntersecting) return;
          entry.target.classList.add("is-visible");
          observer.unobserve(entry.target);
        });
      }, { threshold: 0.16 });
      sections.forEach((section) => observer.observe(section));
    }
    initialiseAboutReveals();
  </script>
</Layout>
